  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Direction ratio&#39;s of the plane perpendicular to two given lines is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>&#160;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>8</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>7</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, plane passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;(A point on the first line),</p><p>Hence, the equation of plane&nbsp;containing lines is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>z</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Foot of perpendicular of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
